# PAN Key/KeyLocation Flow Plan v2 — Stage 3, 4, 5 + Daily Job Run

## 1. Design summary

Two distinct values, never conflated:

| Value | Scope | Purpose | Generated |
|---|---|---|---|
| `keyLocation` | **job-wide** — one value, shared by every chunk | scopes the INDEX counter, PAN dedup, and in-memory PAN↔INDEX cache (`SEQUENTIAL_COUNTER_CACHE`, `PAN_TO_SEQ_INDEX_CACHE`, `FORWARD_CACHE`, `NEW_TO_ORIGINAL_INDEX_CACHE`) | once, in `ChunkGeneratorController.postChunks`, before any chunk dispatches |
| `vaultKeyLocation` | **per-file** — unique to every single `.EncPan.csv` written | the literal Vault AES key path that file's `ENC()` ciphertext is encrypted under; recorded in that file's own `# key-location:` header | freshly, at the moment each `.EncPan.csv` is written |

**Rule of thumb:** `keyLocation` answers *"which job's PAN-index space is this?"* — it must never vary within a job. `vaultKeyLocation` answers *"which Vault secret encrypts this particular file?"* — it must be fresh every time a file is written, chunk-level or job-level.

No entity changes required (per constraint: `Job` cannot get a new field). `keyLocation` is carried only via `ChunkMessage.keyLocation`, set once and copied to every chunk. `vaultKeyLocation` is never carried on any message — it exists only inside the file it encrypts, discovered by reading that file's header.

