## 5. Stage 4 — `WorkerFullfill` (read back, restore, recover if needed)

```java
private void processDtoSegments(EntityManager em, Counts counts, ChunkMessage cm,
                                 Object fileHandleInput, String fileName) {
    try {
        PanDecryptService decryptService = PanDecryptServiceHolder.getInstance();
        boolean vaultEnabled = Objects.nonNull(decryptService) && decryptService.isEnabled();
        String keyLocation = vaultEnabled ? cm.getKeyLocation() : null;
        if (!vaultEnabled) {
            log.info("Vault is disabled");
        }

        boolean keyLocationExists = Objects.nonNull(keyLocation) && !keyLocation.isEmpty();
        if (vaultEnabled && !keyLocationExists) {
            log.error("Vault is enabled but keyLocation is null/empty for chunk [{}] "
                + "aborting fullfill to prevent PAN data integrity issue", cm.getChunkId());
            throw new TucException("keyLocation null/empty with Vault enabled, chunk [" + cm.getChunkId() + "]");
        }

        if (keyLocationExists) {
            // Crash recovery: this chunk's OWN intermediate file, decrypted under
            // ITS OWN header vaultKeyLocation (recoverChunkFromCompanionCsv already
            // reads lookup.getKeyLocation() internally — no change needed there).
            File companion = new File(fileName + ".EncPan.csv");
            boolean companionExists = companion.exists();
            if (companionExists) {
                PanLookup lookup = new EncPanCsvReader().parse(companion.getAbsolutePath());
                Map<String, String> seqToEnc = lookup.getIndexToEncValue();
                boolean allCovered = (seqToEnc != null) && !seqToEnc.isEmpty()
                    && PanSubstitutionService.isFullyCoveredByNewToOriginalMap(keyLocation, seqToEnc.keySet());
                if (!allCovered) {
                    int n = PanSubstitutionService.recoverChunkFromCompanionCsv(fileName, keyLocation);
                    log.info("recovered [{}] mappings for chunk [{}] after restart", n, cm.getChunkId());
                }
            }
        }

        List<Object> dtoSegments;
        while (((dtoSegments = fileio.readPerson(fileHandleInput)) != null) && (!dtoSegments.isEmpty())) {
            em.getTransaction().begin();
            counts.persons++;

            if (keyLocationExists) {
                List<IndicBaseDto> indicDtos = ListDtoHelper.getByType(dtoSegments, "ca.tuc.commons.dto.schema.indic.IndicBaseDto");
                PanRestorationHelper.resolveSeqIndexToRealPan(indicDtos, keyLocation);
            }

            processFullfiller(cm, dtoSegments, counts, em);
            postBilling(cm, dtoSegments);
            postInquiry(cm, dtoSegments);
            counts.inquiryCount++;
            em.getTransaction().commit();
        }
    } catch (Exception e) {
        log.error(StringEscapeUtils.escapeJava("problem while..."), e);
    }
}
```

**No structural change from the earlier version** — `resolveSeqIndexToRealPan` and
`recoverChunkFromCompanionCsv` both already operate correctly under the two-key split
without modification, because `recoverChunkFromCompanionCsv` was already designed to
read the encryption key from the file's own header (`lookup.getKeyLocation()`) rather
than from the parameter passed in. The `keyLocation` parameter there is only used to
reseed the job-wide index-scope caches, which is correct as-is.

