## 8. Daily job run — end-to-end trace with both keys

```
Quartz trigger → ChunkGeneratorController.executeInternal() → run(0)
    for each companyCode: chunksForCompany(company, wd, em)
        determines jobType (REGULAR/FIRSTTIME/ATTPLUS/DEFAULT_BASELINE)
        getNewJob() → persists Job (STATUS_DAILY_ACTIVE) — NO input file, NO companion CSV
        backendDao.buildCfidset(job, wd) → active CfIDs from DB
        backendDao.buildChunks(job, chunkSize=250) → partitions into Chunk records
        postChunks(job, cust, em)
            ★ keyLocation = PanSubstitutionService.generateKeyLocation()   [job-wide, generated ONCE]
            for each Chunk → msg.keyLocation = keyLocation → post to JMS

WorkerFullfill.run(cm) → processDtoSegments(...)
    keyLocation = cm.getKeyLocation()   [same value posted above]
    [crash recovery only if this chunk's .txt.EncPan.csv exists and cache is cold]
    while reading DTOs from the .txt file written by Stage 3:
        PanRestorationHelper.resolveSeqIndexToRealPan(indicDtos, keyLocation)
        processFullfiller → FullfillerDefault.fullfill(cm, dtoSegments, em)
            substituteConsumerRow(..., keyLocation)
            calculateAnetChars() ← realPAN used here
            substituteIndicDtoList(..., keyLocation)
            writeRow() → <chunk>.out   [INDEX only]

SaveTriggeredConsumerDataImpl.saveConsumerData(cm, ...)   [runs earlier, Stage 3, per chunk]
    keyLocation = cm.getKeyLocation()
    substituteAcctNumInRow / substituteAcLinesInBlock(..., keyLocation) → <chunk>.txt   [INDEX only]
    writeIntermediateEncPanCsv(txtPath, keyLocation, ...)
        ★ vaultKeyLocation = PanSubstitutionService.generateKeyLocation()   [per-FILE, fresh]
        buildOutputCiphertextMap(keyLocation, plainPanMap, vaultKeyLocation, decryptService)
        EncPanCsvWriter.write(..., vaultKeyLocation, ...) → <chunk>.txt.EncPan.csv

[after all chunks complete]
ShipfileBuilderImpl.build(job, cust, em)
    assembleShipFile() → concatenates every <chunk>.out into the final .out shipfile
    generateEncPanCsv(custCode, outFileName, job)
        keyLocation = resolveJobKeyLocation(job)   [same job-wide value, throughout]
        plainPanMap = resolvePlainPanMapForOutput(keyLocation, outFileName)   [warm cache, if same-process]
        if warm:
            ★ vaultKeyLocation = PanSubstitutionService.generateKeyLocation()   [per-FILE, fresh, different from every chunk's]
            encryptedMap = buildEncryptedMap(keyLocation, vaultKeyLocation, plainPanMap)
            EncPanCsvWriter.write(..., vaultKeyLocation, ...) → job-level .out.EncPan.csv
            finalizeJob() → PanSubstitutionService.evict(keyLocation)
        else (cache cold — process restarted):
            recoverFromIntermediateCsvs(custCode, outFileName, keyLocation)
                for each <chunk>.txt.EncPan.csv:
                    decrypt under THAT CHUNK'S OWN header vaultKeyLocation → plaintext
                    merge into mergedPlainPan
                ★ vaultKeyLocation = PanSubstitutionService.generateKeyLocation()   [per-FILE, fresh]
                encrypt mergedPlainPan under new vaultKeyLocation
                EncPanCsvWriter.write(..., vaultKeyLocation, ...) → job-level .out.EncPan.csv
```

**Daily job specifics:** no input file, no companion CSV, `keyLocation` is the only
thing driving PAN handling — generated purely from `postChunks` being called, with
zero dependency on any externally-supplied file at any point in Stages 3–5. This is
identical for FIRSTTIME/ATTPLUS/DEFAULT_BASELINE job types — the branching in
`chunksForCompany`/`chunksForCompanyJob` only affects `jobType`/`priority`, never the
PAN key generation logic.

